1
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:48,942
Listen closely now, Sports Maximum.

2
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:51,277
Just as land comprises 30% of the planet

3
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:55,657
and water comprises 70%,

4
00:01:56,199 --> 00:02:00,203
a certain number of souls
are able to inhabit this planet.

5
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:05,542
The more that humans populate this earth,

6
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:10,713
proportionately, fewer of
the other organisms can inhabit it.

7
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:15,343
The total number of souls
constantly remains fixed.

8
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:20,265
Now, let's suppose that
there's a way for one human

9
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:24,644
to possess dozens, no,
hundreds of thousands of souls.

10
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,105
What will this human see?

11
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:32,694
What does the future hold
for such a human?

12
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:37,240
I couldn't even begin to guess.

13
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:41,202
It's an interesting thought, though.

14
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:45,456
So, what is it that you want me to do?

15
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,667
Sports Maximum.

16
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:51,296
I wanted to ask you about this bone.

17
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:55,258
There's something I want you
to try doing to it.

18
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:58,970
Try to revive this bone.

19
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:02,056
Is that a human bone?

20
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,099
Whose is it?

21
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:05,518
That doesn't concern you.

22
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:08,354
Let's just say it belongs to
an old friend of mine.

23
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:13,776
You're telling me to revive it,
but that's just a tiny piece.

24
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:17,155
Or do you mean to tell me that
the entire skeleton is somewhere else?

25
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:20,199
Can a single bone even be revived?

26
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:22,410
Dio…

27
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,371
This is his last remaining bone.

28
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:29,709
The rest of him is dust.
They no longer exist in this world.

29
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:33,046
But you must try, Sports Maximum.

30
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:36,257
If you fail, surely you understand

31
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:39,928
that the ability I bestowed
will no longer be yours.

32
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:42,180
I get that.

33
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:45,183
But I already tried.

34
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:48,770
It's done already.

35
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:58,446
What's happening?

36
00:03:58,529 --> 00:04:01,324
Where is the bone?

37
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:03,785
Where did it go?

38
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:05,245
Where is Dio's bone?

39
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,497
What did you do to it?

40
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,541
Where is his bone? Now tell me!

41
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:13,044
The hell should I know?

42
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:16,547
That's not a normal bone, now, is it?

43
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:28,768
That bone is beyond my ability's control.

44
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:32,230
The bone is moving around by itself.

45
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,984
But I can sense it.

46
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:39,988
I sense it moving around close by.

47
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,573
Search for it! Get going, now!

48
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:47,495
Hold it, Sports Maximum.

49
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:51,582
This proves his theory.

50
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:57,338
There definitely is a way
to get to heaven.

51
00:04:57,422 --> 00:05:00,675
Do not chase the bone. Leave it be.

52
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:04,887
Let his bone wander about freely.

53
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:08,016
I shall merely observe its movements.

54
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,852
Then, I will combine it
with Jotaro Kujo's memory.

55
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:12,979
I will learn the truth!

56
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:18,609
I feel the bone's presence
from the Ultra Security House Unit.

57
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:21,654
Someone may have picked it up.

58
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:31,539
That was Sports Maximum's memory
Ermes retrieved by coincidence.

59
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,791
Of course, Jolyne already watched it.

60
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,627
Then Jolyne got punished on purpose

61
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:41,174
so that she gets confined at
the Disciplinary Wing to find the bone!

62
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:43,593
Yes. But it's too reckless.

63
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:46,846
Pale Snake must be aware that
we read Sports Maximum's memory.

64
00:05:46,929 --> 00:05:49,724
Now, he will do everything
within his power

65
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,142
to eliminate Jolyne.

66
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,646
Jolyne will not last in that wing
by herself.

67
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:59,650
I am able to exist like this
thanks to Jolyne.

68
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:02,612
But I don't know what I can do.

69
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:04,906
I want your help.

70
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:09,660
I can't. Even Weather Forecast,
who is recuperating in the infirmary,

71
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,746
cannot reach that part of the facility.

72
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:15,541
I wish I could help, but…

73
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,753
The Maximum Security Disciplinary Wing,

74
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:23,091
or Ultra Security House Unit,
is southeast of the male wing.

75
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:26,928
To reach it, you must first leave
the premises on a transport car.

76
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:29,097
There are no secret passages there either.

77
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,641
I've never even been there.

78
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:37,355
So I don't know how
I can keep Jolyne safe.

79
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:39,607
I'm not asking you to keep her safe.

80
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:44,362
I only want you to sneak me
inside the Ultra Security House Unit.

81
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:51,577
Hey, is there anything you can do for us?

82
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:53,538
You can't expect him to help.

83
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,248
Anastasia wouldn't cooperate.

84
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:59,335
But isn't he a Stand User?

85
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:01,963
Were you born with your ability?

86
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:10,304
Like I said, don't count on Anastasia.

87
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:13,599
He will not cooperate with anyone,
no matter the reason.

88
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:14,934
Why is that?

89
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:16,686
It's because…

90
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:19,397
I'm willing to do anything.

91
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:23,151
If you take me to
the Ultra Security House Unit,

92
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:26,195
- I'll do anything to repay you--
- Stop, F.F.

93
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:30,158
He just isn't the type of person
who helps others out.

94
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,660
What I'm trying to say is, well…

95
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:37,290
Have you heard of Anastasia, his name?

96
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:40,042
He's a murderer.

97
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:45,506
Anastasia's full name
is Narciso Anastasia.

98
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:49,427
Ever since he was a child,
for some inexplicable reason,

99
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,179
he's had a peculiar habit.

100
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,766
No, not really a habit,
but rather, a syndrome.

101
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:59,812
A syndrome where he has the urge
to disassemble everything.

102
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:02,732
He just must disassemble what he sees.

103
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:06,444
When he was ten, he disassembled
his neighbor's Porsche

104
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:08,446
and was institutionalized for six months.

105
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:12,325
One time, he disassembled
a high-voltage telephone pole.

106
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:16,204
And when he was 21,

107
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:20,374
he went over to
his then girlfriend's apartment.

108
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,962
She was in bed with another man.

109
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:32,512
Anastasia disassembled
their bodies on the spot

110
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,347
so they can never be together again.

111
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:39,560
The psychiatric analysis conducted
after his arrest

112
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:41,020
surprisingly came back normal.

113
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,857
That's how he ended up in the Aquarium.

114
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:48,110
Without Weather Forecast
keeping him under control,

115
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,737
who knows what he's capable of?

116
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,781
That's Anastasia.

117
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,449
So please, give up on him.

118
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:58,788
But I can't reach Jolyne by myself.

119
00:08:58,871 --> 00:09:00,289
I need backup.

120
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:04,877
At the least,
I can't do it without his help.

121
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:06,629
But how strange.

122
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:08,172
This feeling…

123
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:10,424
If he refuses,

124
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:13,553
 I'll try to coerce him into it
with my ability.

125
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:14,470
But…

126
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:19,392
I can't visualize my first shot
successfully hitting him.

127
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,103
I don't even know where to aim for.

128
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:27,608
If I'm not willing to kill him,
he won't listen to me.

129
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:31,904
That's the feeling I get from him,
but still, I must try.

130
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,781
That's the reason why I came.

131
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:37,618
All right. Okay.

132
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:39,870
I can go defend her.

133
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,581
Jolyne Cujoh, that is.

134
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,584
- What?
- I will cooperate.

135
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:51,424
And if she wants to find
that bone or something,

136
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,385
I will help with that too.

137
00:09:55,052 --> 00:09:56,345
Now, let's hurry.

138
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:59,682
She may be under attack as we speak.

139
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:04,812
Hold on, Anastasia!

140
00:10:06,272 --> 00:10:07,898
What are you plotting?

141
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,693
Plotting?

142
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:13,279
I just told you.

143
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:16,073
I will protect her with all my might.

144
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,617
But…

145
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,994
I've taken a liking to her,

146
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:23,414
and everything about her
the moment I laid my eyes on her.

147
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:28,044
She willingly went to the Disciplinary
Wing to save her father.

148
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:31,255
Her conviction charms me even more.

149
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:37,094
If I successfully protect her to the end,
then I will marry her.

150
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,512
This is my condition.

151
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:39,972
Got that?

152
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,766
F.F., was it?

153
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,645
You said you are willing to do anything.

154
00:10:46,145 --> 00:10:48,689
Then, give us your blessing.

155
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:51,317
That's what a wedding needs.

156
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:54,153
What the…

157
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:55,613
Do what now?

158
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,325
He said he'll do what
with Jolyne just now?

159
00:11:04,288 --> 00:11:06,040
Diver Drive!

160
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:22,765
The hell's going on?

161
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:25,309
What was that crash?

162
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:37,488
The attack was delayed,
and it came out of the wall.

163
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:42,910
That's Anastasia's Stand,
Diver Drive's ability.

164
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:48,165
Give us your blessing.

165
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,922
STAND NAME: SURVIVOR
STAND MASTER: GUCCIO

166
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:59,385
Hey, out of curiosity, Dio.

167
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:02,471
Out of all the Stands you've seen,

168
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:06,642
which one was the weakest?

169
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:10,896
It can be one you encountered
while traveling around the world,

170
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:14,108
or one that was created.

171
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,820
Which one, I wonder.

172
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:21,574
What is considered suitable
is different from person to person.

173
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,576
A king has his strengths…

174
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,203
and a cook has his own too.

175
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:29,081
That's what it means to live.

176
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:31,375
The same goes for Stands.

177
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:34,003
The concept of being strong or weak
does not apply.

178
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:36,589
I phrased it badly.

179
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:38,549
Children argue for fun about things like

180
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:41,177
"Which one is stronger,
Stallone and Van Damme?"

181
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:42,761
Let's talk on that level.

182
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:48,851
A Stand I named Survivor is the weakest.

183
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:50,811
However, Survivor is a handful.

184
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:54,064
Survivor? Sounds powerful.

185
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,026
It was 1982.

186
00:12:57,109 --> 00:13:02,031
In France's Lorraine region,
a group of six went hiking,

187
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:05,075
went missing, and then were found dead.

188
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,162
The investigation team stated that

189
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:11,499
the six broke out into a fight
in the mountains.

190
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:15,127
They fought each other to death.

191
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:20,591
Men and women alike applied
such intense force to their muscles

192
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,760
that their own bones broke.

193
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:24,970
A tooth that broke
and flew off after a punch

194
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:27,681
had split a rock and wedged itself there.

195
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:29,725
That's how brutal the struggle was.

196
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:35,523
Even the victor was unable to descend
the mountain due to his injuries.

197
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:39,443
Here is what I learned later.

198
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:42,905
The six had stayed in a lodge
the night before they died.

199
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:45,699
They had quarreled with the lodge owner.

200
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:47,326
One of the women

201
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:51,413
ridiculed the lodge owner's body odor,
saying he stunk.

202
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:54,750
And this lodge owner was a Stand User.

203
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:56,001
Precisely.

204
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:58,462
But what did this lodge owner do to them?

205
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:01,131
And why did the six fight to their deaths?

206
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,969
The answer is that he did nothing.

207
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:08,973
He did nothing to them,
but there was a slight anger

208
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,934
that surged in his mind.

209
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:13,561
And that slight anger

210
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:16,855
converted into a small
electric potential in his brain,

211
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:22,111
traveled down his nervous system,
and flowed out into the ground.

212
00:14:23,862 --> 00:14:25,406
That's the Stand, Survivor.

213
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:28,742
The electric current followed
the ground's surface

214
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:30,911
all the way to the six hikers.

215
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:34,039
The ground and the hikers' shoes
had to be wet

216
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,208
to let the electricity travel easily.

217
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:41,005
The electric potential sending
signals to the nervous system

218
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:43,299
is very small, at 70mV.

219
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:45,926
This Stand dwells in
that slight pulse of energy.

220
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:51,557
Survivor's attack is mostly unnoticed,
and it doesn't cause any harm.

221
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:56,061
It does not injure humans,
nor can it manipulate them.

222
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:59,148
It cannot inflict pain
or put someone to sleep.

223
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:01,692
The Stand does none of these things.

224
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,904
It simply awakens its victim's anger.

225
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:09,992
It stimulates the limbic system
of the human brain ever so slightly,

226
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:13,120
awakening its fighting spirit.

227
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:17,541
Just because one woman
ridiculed the lodge owner's body odor,

228
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,169
all six were made
to fight to their deaths.

229
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:27,468
Earlier, you said it's a handful.

230
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:30,262
A useless Stand is what it is.

231
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,765
It can't tell a friend from foe.

232
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:35,726
If subordinates
started fighting each other,

233
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:37,394
their organization would collapse.

234
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:42,066
Could you give me that ability?

235
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:45,653
If you don't plan on using it,
I'll take just the Stand.

236
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:50,491
Extract the ability only
and store it in a disc, you say?

237
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,451
That may be a good idea.

238
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:54,286
To each their own.

239
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:58,207
It may prove useful one of these days.

240
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:07,091
I guess these mushrooms are edible.

241
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:10,094
They're pretty good.

242
00:16:13,889 --> 00:16:15,766
It's shower time.

243
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:18,560
Get up, FE40536!

244
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,233
It's bright!

245
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:27,277
Hell yeah! I got her!

246
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,821
She hid!

247
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:31,281
She hid like a dirty cockroach!

248
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,283
I win this cell.

249
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:35,703
The total sum is 20 dollars for my wins!

250
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:37,287
Sorry!

251
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:41,375
Damn. But all I got on me is 15 dollars.

252
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:43,252
Come on, let's shake on it.

253
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:45,337
If that's all you got, I guess.

254
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:49,258
In any case,

255
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:54,930
what I must do here
is to use this thread to find the bone.

256
00:16:55,931 --> 00:16:57,641
What is that bone doing here?

257
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:00,477
I don't know the answer yet,

258
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:05,357
but for some reason, it's somewhere
inside this Disciplinary Wing.

259
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:09,069
Could it be in someone's possession?

260
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:14,033
If I can obtain the bone first,
Pale Snake will come after me.

261
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,200
And with him,

262
00:17:15,993 --> 00:17:20,289
my father's stolen memory disc
in his hand!

263
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:21,790
Hey dumbass!

264
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,500
Who told you to stand?

265
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:30,883
By the way,

266
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:34,011
how do you think
the Marlins will play tonight?

267
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,637
Their chances of winning are slim.

268
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:39,099
The pitcher broke up
with that reporter girl.

269
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,851
He won't throw any strikes.

270
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:43,645
You want to bet those 15 dollars on it?

271
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,856
I'm in.

272
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:48,275
Aren't you short on money, though?

273
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:50,486
I'm telling you, his throws will be bad.

274
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,614
No, that pitcher is good.

275
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:55,741
You're such easy prey.

276
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,411
Can't wait for tonight's game.

277
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,461
Oh, sorry.

278
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:09,254
This valve doesn't close very easily.

279
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:11,006
Be more careful.

280
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:15,344
I have to go back to the main prison
to change.

281
00:18:21,058 --> 00:18:23,268
Hey, why did you hit me?

282
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:24,978
I said I'm sorry.

283
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:27,397
It's not like I got you wet on purpose.

284
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:30,818
Oh, did I hit you just now?

285
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,490
The hell is wrong with you?

286
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:38,867
I didn't smack you that hard.

287
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:41,120
You want some?

288
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:45,207
You didn't need to punch me hard, bastard.

289
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,712
- You jerk!
- Asshole!

290
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:52,673
Why you little…

291
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,800
All right, that's enough.

292
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:56,218
I said enough.

293
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:57,511
I said stop.

294
00:18:57,594 --> 00:18:59,763
I'll apologize. I'm sorry.

295
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:02,558
I'll lend you my uniform
if you don't have a spare.

296
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:06,019
That settles it, right? Let's be done.

297
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:09,898
What got into you? Calm down.

298
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,985
Are you in a bad mood today?

299
00:19:13,068 --> 00:19:18,615
We're friends… right?

300
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:21,785
That hurts!

301
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:27,791
You swing hard, fucker!

302
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,293
I'll take you on!

303
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:31,795
What has gotten into them?

304
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:34,131
It can't be…

305
00:19:35,465 --> 00:19:36,884
I'm getting excited.

306
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,469
His physique…

307
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:42,723
I can see where his body's strengths are!

308
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:45,434
His superbly developed muscles!

309
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,477
Beautiful…

310
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:51,982
I can sense
his strongest muscle structures!

311
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:55,152
How wonderful it is to fight!

312
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,029
What the…

313
00:19:57,112 --> 00:19:58,989
What's happening to their bodies?

314
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:01,617
What are those things that seem to shine?

315
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:07,956
Here I come.
I'll show you who is stronger!

316
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:27,559
I am the strongest!

317
00:20:29,853 --> 00:20:32,522
Is this an enemy's attack?

318
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:34,816
Is that guard my foe?

319
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:38,278
No, the enemy hasn't shown up yet.

320
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:41,240
But this is a Stand ability!

321
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:44,159
This freakish feel…
It must be a Stand attack!

322
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,704
"Do not cast what is holy to the dogs;

323
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:50,290
lest they trample them under their feet,

324
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:54,419
and turn and tear you in pieces."

325
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,756
Matthew 7:6.

326
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:00,884
Sports Maximum has gone missing.

327
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:03,845
I can't fathom how they learned of it,

328
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:09,059
but I must conclude that
they read his memory.

329
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:13,188
The number of Stand Users
I sent to the Disciplinary Wing…

330
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:14,773
Four!

331
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:20,320
If Jolyne Cujoh entered
the Disciplinary Wing

332
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:23,240
in search of Dio's bone…

333
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:30,914
I cannot let her live a moment longer.

334
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,333
I will use all my strength
to eliminate her!

335
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:36,878
It doesn't really matter what happens
inside the Disciplinary Wing.

336
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:39,214
Those four will undoubtedly fight on

337
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:44,720
until Jotaro's daughter is eliminated!

338
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,473
He sent everything he's got.

339
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:57,316
I can see where your strengths are!

340
00:21:57,899 --> 00:21:59,609
Bastards!

341
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:03,280
I can see

342
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:08,160
the strongest parts
of each fighter's body from here!

343
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,871
It's Fight Club time!

344
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:13,623
Let's brawl!

345
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
